------------------------            MODULES            ------------------------

formats.py
	Module containing functions for dealing with I/O and specific formats
	Includes a class & function for iterating over GFF files, among other stuff

libintrons.py
	Module containing code for dealing with intron scoring & selection
	Chiefly includes the GenomicSequence class (& subclasses), as well as
	functions for deserializing GFF files to GenomicSequence subclasses and
	scoring	introns
	Indirectly import formats.py

sequtils.py
	Module containing one-off functions for examining nucleotide sequences



------------------------            SCRIPTS            ------------------------

add_introns.py
	Given a GFF, interpose introns between each pair of exons
	If the GFF's referened FASTA is supplied, the introns will have their
	splice sites denoted under the "splice_site" attribute

find_altseq_gff.py
	Given a GFF+FASTA and a file containing grouped genes, find pairs of
	transcript sequences which came from the same transcript

find_altseq_fa.py
	Like find_altseq_fa.py, but takes only a FASTA file as input, and compares
	all unique pairs of sequences in the file

find_mrna_mismatches.py
	Given a transcriptome-to-genome mapping GFF, a genome FASTA and a
	transcriptome FASTA, find mappings whose sequences do not match the
	original transcript sequence

get_orf_len.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, report the length of each transcript's longest ORF

rectify_introns.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, find and score all intron variants, then select the
	best variant for each intron

get_gene_scores.py
	Report the "avg_intron_score" attribute for every gene in a GFF file

introns_corn.py
	Given a GFF, mark each intron possessing a "splice_site" attribute as
	conventional or nonconventional, based on the splice site sequence

subset_gff.py
	Given a GFF & a list of feature IDs, subset the GFF file to exclude/include
	the listed features and all of their children
	Assumes every feature in the GFF with a Parent attribute comes after its
	parent
	